<Layout title="Sponsor policy — Cramzz Lab" description="The creative, safety, disclosure, payment, and measurement rules for every Cramzz sponsorship.">
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Trust / Sponsor policy</p><h1 class="page-title">Useful context, never camouflage.</h1><p class="page-intro">Sponsor support should make an experiment possible without making the experience less trustworthy.</p></div></header>
  <div class="shell prose-wrap">
    <aside class="prose-nav"><span>Sponsors</span><a href="#principles">Principles</a><a href="#prohibited">Prohibited</a><a href="#creative">Creative review</a><a href="#measurement">Measurement</a><a href="#payments">Payments</a></aside>
    <article class="prose"><p class="legal-updated">Effective 20 September 2026</p>
      <section id="principles"><h2>Non-negotiable principles</h2><ul><li>Every paid placement is plainly labelled “Sponsored”.</li><li>A sponsor cannot influence a player’s score, odds, puzzle answer, or access to core functionality.</li><li>Shared result cards do not imply that the player endorses a sponsor.</li><li>We do not promise audience size or outcomes that have not already been measured.</li><li>Sponsorship does not grant editorial control over Cramzz findings.</li></ul></section>
      <section id="prohibited"><h2>Prohibited categories and behavior</h2><p>We reject malware, deceptive redirects, impersonation, adult sexual content, gambling, political persuasion, hate or harassment, counterfeit goods, illegal products, unlicensed financial promotions, misleading health claims, and material that infringes another party’s rights. We may reject any placement that creates a safety, trust, or legal concern.</p></section>
      <section id="creative"><h2>Creative and destination review</h2><p>The sponsor must control or be authorized to use its submitted name, logo, claims, and link. We inspect the destination before approval and may re-check it while the placement is live. Changing an approved destination to materially different content can pause the placement without notice.</p><p>Creative must remain readable, accurately represent the sponsor, and fit the experiment without obstructing controls or accessibility.</p></section>
      <section id="measurement"><h2>Measurement and reporting</h2><p>Reports use aggregate experiment events such as views, completions, and shares. We do not give sponsors visitor identities, behavioral profiles, payment details, or raw device-level logs. Early packages may have little or no reach; unlock thresholds prevent us from selling larger packages prematurely.</p></section>
      <section id="payments"><h2>Approval, payment, and activation</h2><ol><li>Submit a sponsor brief.</li><li>Receive written creative and package approval.</li><li>Pay only through the individual Razorpay Payment Link supplied for that approved brief.</li><li>Wait for manual confirmation that payment is captured and the placement is scheduled.</li></ol><div class="callout">A successful redirect to Cramzz is not a receipt and does not activate a placement.</div></section>
      <section><h2>Removal and remedies</h2><p>We may pause or remove a placement that violates this policy, becomes unsafe, or is required to be removed by law or a platform provider. Refund or rescheduling terms for a Cramzz-caused failure will be agreed in the package confirmation; violations by the sponsor may not be refundable.</p></section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
